{
    "repo": "swaywm/sway",
    "pr_number": 1648,
    "lang": "c",
    "pr_title": "Port swaybar to layer shell",
    "pr_body": "I overhauled swaybar's rendering stack along the way.\r\n\r\nFixes #1645, fixes #1224, fixes #1352, fixes #771, fixes #554, fixes #552\r\n\r\n* [x] swaybar\r\n  * [x] Port to layer surfaces\r\n  * [x] Overhaul rendering\r\n  * [x] IPC\r\n  * [x] text mode status line\r\n* [x] sway\r\n  * [x] bar configuration\r\n  * [x] IPC get_bar_config\r\n  * [x] IPC get_workspaces\r\n  * [x] Emit workspace events\r\n  * [x] Spawn i3bar process\r\n  * [x] Config reloading\r\n  * [x] avoid rearranging all windows all the time (layer shell issue)\r\n  * [x] Rearrange on config reload\r\n\r\nNot doing in this patch:\r\n\r\n* [ ] hidpi\r\n* [ ] input\r\n* [ ] output hotplugging\r\n* [ ]  i3bar json status line\r\n* [ ] tray",
    "pr_comments": [
        "This is ready for review."
    ],
    "merged": true,
    "created_at": "2018-03-30T02:00:25Z",
    "issue_context": {
        "number": 554,
        "title": "Lack of vertical alignment for swaybar",
        "body": "I noticed bar elements aren't vertically centered:\n![sway](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1748909/14128269/e95707d6-f67b-11e5-9828-432667ae9cdc.png)\n\ni3 version for reference:\n![i3](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/1748909/14128271/ef47755e-f67b-11e5-9886-9ba648c5e41d.png)\n",
        "comments": [
            "By the way (maybe this should be a separate issue), @SirCmpwn, would it be possible to add a \"true center\" (and maybe left) alignment so that swaybar sections wouldn't all have to be right-aligned? This is distinct from the current align-within-maximum-width option.\n",
            "I'm not entirely open to that idea right now, but if you make a seperate issue maybe it'll happen in the future.\n",
            "@beanaroo can you post your configs so I can try to replicate the issue?\n",
            "I have my i3 configuration up on github [over here.](https://github.com/beanaroo/dotfiles/tree/master/.config/i3).\n\nI did not make a backup of the sway config, but will post as soon as I can.\n",
            "Strange, it looks pretty much aligned here:\n\n![swaybar](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/128566/14899317/bc89d914-0d8b-11e6-9b52-422c149d2c95.png)\n",
            "interesting, I'll try again today.\n",
            "@mikkeloscar After reinstalling Arch and sway, the status line is now vertically centered. The workspace indicators, however, are not. Unlike the screenshot you posted. This is obvious when a binding mode indicator is present, which is centered.\n\nI tested multiple fonts, sizes and heights just to be sure.\n",
            "Well, checked this, because It looks like it was not centered for me.\nActually it IS vertically centered, but: it is centered for your swaybar font. And it is not possible to use pango in workspace icons, so your swaybar font is font with icons. I think that you use another font for text on your swaybar (for the date, for example), using pango, just as I am. Second, normal font is not vertically centered \u2014 because it is aligned in the other way, it's baseline is equal to the baseline of default swaybar font (which is font with icons).\nChecked with one font for all bar \u2014 and yes, everything is vertically centered.\nSo it is not a swaybar bug.\n"
        ]
    },
